# The ending an_empty_car (data/endings/an_empty_car.json): the narration the ending screen plays before its slides. The Vagrant tells it
# afterwards: second person, present tense, one or two sentences a line, no game words. First draft by Claude; Gemini edits it.

~ start
Narrator: One after another you step up to the goat skull and give it the only thing it can't refuse, and the moon takes the Crooked Queen and keeps her.
Narrator: The Crooked Tree burns on an empty hill, with nobody left to watch it.
Narrator: Days later a whistle comes out of the mist at the old platform, and the Ghostlight Express rolls in and opens every door.
the_vagrant: Four tickets on the board and not a soul to punch them. Well. That's a brave way to end a song.
Narrator: The doors close, and the train pulls out with every car lit and every seat empty.
